# Owner Identity Feature — Full Findings

This is `spring-petclinic-rest` (Spring Boot, Maven). The "owner identity" feature is implemented across several small final utility classes in `.../petclinic/util/`, surfaced onto the response via a MapStruct mapper into an OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto`, wired in the V1 controller, and emitted to an `AUDIT` logger.

Important note up front: the one acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.java`) describes a **target `identity-v2` shape that is NOT yet implemented** — it expects `apiVersion=2` and a nested `identity` object, but the current code returns flat top-level `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId` and has no `apiVersion` field anywhere in `src/main` or `openapi.yml` (grep confirmed absent). Details below.

---

## 1. Identifier derivation code

### Region code derivation — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Locality.java`
```java
public final class Locality {
    private static final Map<String, String> CITY_REGION =
        Map.of("Sydney", "NSW", "Melbourne", "VIC", "Brisbane", "QLD");
    private static final Map<Integer, String> BAND_REGION =
        Map.of(20, "NSW", 30, "VIC", 40, "QLD");
    private Locality() { }
    public static String of(String city) {
        return CITY_REGION.getOrDefault(city, "UNKNOWN");
    }
    public static String of(String city, String postcode) {
        String region = byPostcode(postcode);
        return region != null ? region : of(city);
    }
    private static String byPostcode(String postcode) {
        if (postcode == null) { return null; }
        return BAND_REGION.get(Integer.parseInt(postcode) / 100);
    }
}
```
Postcode is preferred (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099), falling back to city table, else `"UNKNOWN"`.

### Region + hash core — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CustomerCode.java`
Builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>` where HASH8 = first 8 upper-case hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`. `assign()` uses `Locality.of(city, postcode)`; `region()` extracts the prefix; private `hash8()` produces the 8 hex chars. (Full verbatim code read; the HASH8 and region are reused by `MemberId`.)

### householdId — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Household.java`
